{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/126467-worth-picking-up-now-where-to-begin","id":126467,"title":"Worth picking up now/where to begin?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-05-05T22:34:43-07:00","id":126467,"title":"Worth picking up now/where to begin?","content":"I already expect everyone here to tell me this is worth getting at least some of the PDFs on DTRPG, but I'm asking anyway. Whilst we can't predict what the Aeon 2E is going to be like, is it worth starting with Trini or Abberant? I like something with a nice chunk of fluff to it as well as just rules, and there's so many PDFs I can't tell which is the base book for Abberrant or Trinity, so can anyone recommend a good place to start? Thanks guys!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/833-scornednerdvana","name":"ScornedNerdvana","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-06T07:50:06-07:00","id":126687,"title":"","content":"You can find the Trinity corebook here: <a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/product/3407/Trinity-Rulebook?it=1\" target=\"_blank\">http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/produc...-Rulebook?it=1</a><br /> And, the Aberrant corebook here: <a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/product/3/Aberrant-Rulebook?it=1\" target=\"_blank\">http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/produc...-Rulebook?it=1</a><br /> Also, Adventure! can be found here: <a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/product/5/Adventure-Rulebook?it=1\" target=\"_blank\">http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/produc...-Rulebook?it=1</a><br /> <br /> I recommend starting with Trinity or Adventure!, but that's mainly because I like them more. All of the books have a lot of good fluff and setting material, and Adventure! is one of the best RPGs ever produced. Seriously, it's sublime lightning in a bottle.<br /> <br /> -Slag","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6-slagheap","name":"Slagheap","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"188"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-07T08:06:03-07:00","id":127475,"title":"","content":"\u200bAberrant is my recommendation, in contrast to Slagheap.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-07T15:38:05-07:00","id":127784,"title":"","content":"Vote for starting with Trinity here (or, if sci-fi's not your thing then Adventure! is a good second starting point). Aberrant always felt a little out of place compared to the others. But, they each stand on their own quite capably so it comes down to what flavor of game you're looking for <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#ff0000\"><b>Ad Astra</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/232-chill","name":"CHILL","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar232_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-07T23:12:57-07:00","id":128020,"title":"","content":"I started out with Aberrant then added Trinity to the mix of things my group was playing. If you want really over the top stuff Aberrant is the one to start with though Trinity is much better balanced and smoother in play. If you go with Aberrant just do not expect standard four color comic style, it is more of a high powered but narrow concept like the X-Men movies or near future sci-fi with superpowers instead since everything revolves around the same power source.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/869-bc001","name":"BC001","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar869_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}